          "term": "دَقَّة",
          "pronunciation": "daqqaẗ",
          "definition": "a single knock, stroke, or instance"
        }
      ],
      "etymology_notes": null,
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text_en": "sometimes, at times, once",
          "text_mt": "Minn żmien għal żmien, f'okkażjoni waħda jew f'xi waqtiet mhux regolari.",
          "register": "standard",
          "nuance": ""
        }
      ],
      "usage_examples": [
        {
          "mt": "Daqqa joħroġ ix-xemx u daqqa tagħmel ix-xita.",
          "en": "Sometimes the sun comes out and sometimes it rains.",
          "text_mt": "Daqqa joħroġ ix-xemx u daqqa tagħmel ix-xita.",
          "text_en": "Sometimes the sun comes out and sometimes it rains."
        }
      ],
      "usage_notes": {
        "mt": "Spiss jintuża mtenni bħala 'daqqa ... daqqa ...' ('sometimes ... sometimes ...'). Għas-sens ta' 'daqqa ta' sieq' jew 'ħabta', ara n-nom 'daqqa'.",
        "en": "Frequently paired correlatively as 'daqqa ... daqqa ...' ('now ... now ...', 'sometimes ... sometimes ...'). Distinct from the noun 'daqqa' ('blow, strike, time')."
      },
      "phonetics": [
